      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. 17-647"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The critical issue in this case is this: When is an invasion of property without just compensation in violation of the Just Compensation Clause so that a property owner can claim an unconstitutional taking requiring damages? The understanding adopted well before Williamson County and Dow and other cases is that the invasion itself gives rise to a constitutionally rooted claim for compensation, unless, as in Cherokee Nation, the government recognizes the owner's entitlement to compensation and provides a process for collecting it at the time of the invasion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: And, B, why is\nadministrative exhaustion, ripeness okay, but\nnot the same thing if someone goes into state\ncourt to get a final decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But this, General, is -- is -- this is what you argued the first time, that a property owner is deprived of a constitutional right even before the constitutional violation has taken place, is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, but -- well, but that right there seems to give the lie to your argument. You just talked about the deprivation of their property from the moment it was taken."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: An implicit premise of your argument and Petitioner's argument for overruling Williamson County, I think, is that the state courts aren't as good as the federal courts. Why is that, in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is there -- is -- is there some kind of middle position here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What counts as speedy in the Pennsylvania court system?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Would the property owner be entitled to attorneys' fees if the property owner prevailed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you have any -- have you given any thought to the possibility that if you lose this case, that a 1983 plaintiff could go into federal court and enjoin the municipality from enforcing a regulation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Section 1983 provides remedies coextensive with the Fourteenth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "please the Court: I want to talk about state courts real quickly. One of the problems in just saying, well, it's a wash and you can bring your Fifth Amendment claim in state court, so what's the problem, is you can't bring your Fifth Amendment claim in a state court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Is the substance of the claim any different from the takings claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-647",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "67889625f290e7922d3f47aa6dcca3b9396aa453e868f7ec9304506e6652dca5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-67889625f290-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
